{%- comment -%}
  Renders the trailing arrow used on call-to-action buttons and editorial links.

  Source: phase-3-assets/icons/icon-arrow.svg, drawn in Phase 3 to the Phase 2
  contract — 24x24 canvas, stroke 1.5, currentColor, round caps and joins.

  Accepts:
  - class: {String} optional extra class names

  Usage:
  {% render 'icon-arrow', class: 'icon--sm' %}

  This replaces the prototype's literal "→" glyph. Phase 2 section 10.4 records
  why: Jost carries neither U+2192 nor U+20B1, so the glyph falls back to a
  per-platform face and the arrow's weight and baseline shift between devices.
  Trailing affordances are inline SVG in currentColor, hidden from assistive
  technology, because the button's label already says where it goes.
{%- endcomment -%}
<svg class="icon icon--arrow {{ class }}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12h15.5"/><path d="M13.5 6 19.5 12l-6 6"/></svg>
